From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: filter inactive associated station rows

After a silent BTM roam mac80211_hwsim can retain an authorized station row
on the old AP.  A station dump therefore reports the client on both the old
and current AP even though the simulated STA has one serving BSSID.  The
Banana Pi diagnostic provider exports every dumped row, OneWifi marks each
one active, and EasyMesh receives contradictory Associated Clients TLVs.

Use the standard NL80211_STA_INFO_INACTIVE_TIME observation while constructing
the hwsim station snapshot.  Do not export a row which has received no frame
for two minutes.  The deliberately conservative interval does not hide a
legitimately idle simulated client from an authoritative EasyMesh snapshot,
while retained old-AP rows still age out in bounded time.  This is compiled
only for HWSIM_RADIO; physical targets retain their native station-table
semantics and inactivity policy.

The HAL does not delete the kernel row.  It corrects the provider contract:
wifi_getApAssociatedDeviceDiagnosticResult3() returns currently associated
devices, not historical hwsim station objects.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 platform/banana-pi/platform.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/platform/banana-pi/platform.c b/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
index 236ebc3..4980ae8 100644
--- a/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
+++ b/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
@@ -48,5 +48,9 @@
 #define INVALID_KEY  "12345678"
 
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+#define HWSIM_ASSOC_STALE_MSEC 120000U
+#endif
+
 int wifi_nvram_defaultRead(char *in,char *out);
 int _syscmd(char *cmd, char *retBuf, int retBufSize);
 
@@ -686,6 +690,12 @@ static int get_sta_list_handler(struct nl_msg *msg, void *arg)
 {
     struct nlattr *tb[NL80211_ATTR_MAX + 1];
     struct genlmsghdr *gnlh = nlmsg_data(nlmsg_hdr(msg));
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+    struct nlattr *stats[NL80211_STA_INFO_MAX + 1];
+    static struct nla_policy stats_policy[NL80211_STA_INFO_MAX + 1] = {
+        [NL80211_STA_INFO_INACTIVE_TIME] = { .type = NLA_U32 },
+    };
+#endif
     sta_entry_t *entries;
     unsigned int i;
     sta_list_t *sta_list = (sta_list_t *)arg;
@@ -696,6 +706,22 @@ static int get_sta_list_handler(struct nl_msg *msg, void *arg)
         return NL_SKIP;
     }
 
+#ifdef HWSIM_RADIO
+    /* A hwsim STA can leave an authorized station object behind when it
+     * silently reassociates to another virtual AP.  Such an object is useful
+     * kernel history, but it is not a current associated device. */
+    if (tb[NL80211_ATTR_STA_INFO] != NULL &&
+        nla_parse_nested(stats, NL80211_STA_INFO_MAX,
+            tb[NL80211_ATTR_STA_INFO], stats_policy) == 0 &&
+        stats[NL80211_STA_INFO_INACTIVE_TIME] != NULL &&
+        nla_get_u32(stats[NL80211_STA_INFO_INACTIVE_TIME]) >
+            HWSIM_ASSOC_STALE_MSEC) {
+        wifi_hal_stats_dbg_print("%s:%d Skip inactive hwsim station row\n",
+            __func__, __LINE__);
+        return NL_OK;
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (tb[NL80211_ATTR_MAC]) {
         for (i = 0; i < sta_list->num; i++) {
             if (memcmp(sta_list->entries[i].mac, nla_data(tb[NL80211_ATTR_MAC]),
